# Election Module — Registered Bye-Laws (Controlling Source)

IMPORTANT: The Society's attached registered bye-laws are the controlling source for the Election Module. Do not use generic apartment-election assumptions where they conflict with these bye-laws.

## Revised 30-flat configuration

| Rule | Bye-law position |
|------|------------------|
| Apartments | 30 |
| Management Committee | 7 |
| President | 1 |
| Vice-President | 1 |
| Secretary | 1 |
| Treasurer | 1 |
| Executive Members | 3 |
| Committee term | 2 years |
| Re-election | Permitted |
| Member voting right | 1 per member |
| Joint owners | One designated member |
| Proxy | Permitted |
| Proxy deadline | 48 hours before meeting |
| Max proxies/person | 1 member |
| Election quorum | 3/4 (= 23 of 30) |
| Maintenance arrears disqualification | >60 days on election date |
| Voting method | Secret ballot / show of hands (record method before polling) |
| Committee meeting quorum | 2/3 (= 5 of 7) |
| Regular committee meetings | At least monthly |
| Regular meeting notice | 7 clear days |
| First committee meeting | Within 30 days of election |
| Committee vacancy | Majority of remaining committee |
| Committee removal | Special Resolution + hearing |
| Removal disqualification | 2 years |

## Hard constraints

- Do **not** automatically provide separate votes for every office unless that voting method is expressly established/approved. Respect one-member-one-vote.
- Do **not** automatically make second- or third-place candidates members of the Management Committee.
- Do **not** use ranked/Borda "rank every candidate" as the default member UX.
- Vacancies, removals, resignations, adjourned and emergency meetings must follow bye-law procedures exactly.
- Do **not** delete or modify existing Society data; use database migrations.
- Every election-critical action must be auditable.
- Votes must not be editable by ordinary administrators after submission.
- Prevent duplicate voting; maintain an immutable election record.
- Generate a complete Election Report and AGM Election Minutes after completion.

